  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 144 AM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nModel blends suggest the aforementioned frontal boundary stalls over\nKansas. However, a few deterministic models (NAM/GFS) indicate the\nfront could sag into northwest Oklahoma late Tuesday and remain in\nthe area for a few days. As a result, there is at least a low chance\nof showers/storms (15%) over northern Oklahoma on Wednesday through\nThursday with chances in that vicinity rising to near 30% on Thursday\nevening.\n\nGiven the uncertainty in frontal placement and rain chances, temperature\nbloxplots for these locations widen beginning Wednesday. Still, heat\nis expected to persist for the majority of the area and humidity rises\nmiddle to end of next week as dewpoint temperatures rise into the 60's\nand low 70's. Heat headlines are possible for portions of the area\nWednesday through Saturday.\n\nThompson",
